{"name":"Metal Spark","hex":"#eeff99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"metal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Chemical elements or alloys, their ores, and the mines where their ores come from.\n Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity.\n\n Any material with similar physical properties as those chemical elements, especially as a combination of several of them, such as an alloy.\n\n An element which was not directly created after the Big Bang but instead formed through nuclear reactions; any element other than hydrogen and helium.\n\n Crushed rock, stones etc. used to make a road.\n\n The ore from which a metal is derived.\n A mine from which ores are taken.","Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by strong drum-beats and distorted guitars. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Having the emotional or social characteristics associated with metal music; brash, bold, frank, unyielding, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metal"},{"term":"spark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small particle of glowing matter, either molten or on fire, resulting from an electrical surge or excessive heat created by friction.","A short or small burst of electrical discharge."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To trigger, kindle into activity (an argument, etc).","To light; to kindle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spark"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spark (fire)","blocks":[{"text":"A spark is an incandescent particle. Sparks may be produced by pyrotechnics, by metalworking or as a by-product of fires, especially when burning wood."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Sparks_from_a_Grinder.jpg/330px-Sparks_from_a_Grinder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spark_(fire)","wikidata":"Q911679"},{"title":"Metal","blocks":[{"text":"A metal is a material that, when polished or fractured, shows a lustrous appearance, and conducts electricity and heat relatively well. These properties are all associated with having electrons available at the Fermi level, as opposed to nonmetallic materials which do not. Metals are typically ductile and malleable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal","wikidata":"Q11426"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Sparkler.JPG/500px-Sparkler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Sparkler.JPG/1280px-Sparkler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Sparkler.JPG/500px-Sparkler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sparks from a pyrotechnic sparkler.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASparkler.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Erbium_sparks.jpg/500px-Erbium_sparks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Erbium_sparks.jpg/1280px-Erbium_sparks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Erbium_sparks.jpg/500px-Erbium_sparks.jpg?utm_source=